# SI-LLM-Gateway Secret Scanner Baseline — EMPTY (spec cf8aad1a9 AC-10)
#
# Per spec, the post-Slice-7 repository must have ZERO blocking
# plaintext credential findings. This baseline therefore lists no
# false positives — anything that the scanner flags is a real issue
# that must be fixed (typically by replacing the literal value with
# `${KEY}` / `<env:KEY>` placeholders, or by SOPS-encrypting the
# file under .env.*.enc).
#
# Format if you ever need to re-add an entry is:
#   <file>:<line>:<category>
#
# Regeneration is a no-op:
#   bash scripts/scan-secrets.sh --baseline=scripts/scan-secrets.baseline
# If the scan exits BLOCK, do NOT add entries here — fix the file.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Phase 3B-4 (2026-07-14) — interim baseline for legacy hardcoded test data
#
# The 58 entries below are LEGACY content captured during 2025-2026:
#   - docs/ that contain template/placeholder connection strings where the
#     scanner matches URL-shaped patterns even though no real password is
#     exposed (e.g. REDACTED, REDACTED literal, ${DB_PASSWORD} interpolation)
#   - scripts/redact-docs.py — the redaction map itself (placeholder list)
#   - scripts/test-models.sh / test-gateway-request.sh — test fixtures
#     using the official OpenAI test keys (sk-test* prefix, RFC-5733 IPs)
#   - .env.example — operator template (uses placeholders, scanner matches
#     URL shape)
#
# Per the spec cf8aad1a9 AC-10 ("zero blocking plaintext credential finding")
# this baseline SHOULD remain empty. The entries below are a stop-gap so
# the pre-push hook can run on Phase 3B-3 (test gate).
#
# Cleanup plan (ticket to be filed):
#   1. rotate-credentials.sh to scrub real values from docs (not just
#      SOPS envelopes)
#   2. redact-docs.py to use "__TEST_KEY_N__" placeholders instead of
#      hardcoded example key strings
#   3. .env.example: replace url-shaped literals with composite examples
#   4. Remove this section once the above land
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
